{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 ReaBackground\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shows a muted video (synced to the play and edit cursor) or a still image behind REAPER's arrange view on macOS. Items, grid, cursors and overlays stay on top; the time selection, mute shading and grid lines read as shading over the video.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After installing, restart REAPER, then run the action {\b ReaBackground.lua} (or Extensions > ReaBackground...) to open the settings window. Import a video or image with the + tile, click a thumbnail to use it in the current project, or the globe icon to make it the default for every project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requirements: macOS 11 or newer, REAPER with Metal rendering enabled, ReaImGui (install it from ReaPack) for the settings window.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 ReaNotes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A dockable notes window that shows the note for whatever you touched last: a track, a media item or a plug-in. Track notes are saved in the project. Item notes are saved on the item, so duplicates, copies and splits carry their own copy. FX notes are saved once per plug-in and show up in every project that uses it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes are markdown, styled as you type: headings, bold, italic, lists, code, quotes and links (Cmd+click to open).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After installing, restart REAPER, then run the action {\b ReaNotes: Show/hide notes window} (or Extensions > ReaNotes). Right-click the header to dock or undock the window.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requirements: macOS 11 or newer, REAPER 7 or newer.\par}
}
